      <symbol id="i-down-right" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M5 5l13 13M18 8v10H8" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></symbol>
      <symbol id="i-check" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/><path d="M7.6 12.4l3 3 5.8-6.2" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></symbol>
          <symbol id="i-up-right" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M6 18L18 6M8 6h10v10" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></symbol>
    </svg>

    <section class="hero hero-about hero-services hero-legal hero-case" aria-labelledby="case-title">
      <span class="hbar hbar-1" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="hbar hbar-2" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="hbar hbar-3" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="hbar hbar-4" aria-hidden="true"></span>

      <div class="ah-copy">
        <p class="ah-label" data-reveal>Case study</p>
        <h1 id="case-title" data-speakable>
          <span class="line">Interior</span><span class="line">Design Website</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="ah-intro" data-reveal data-speakable>A website concept for an interior design studio</p>
      </div>

      <div class="svc-index cs-meta" role="group" aria-label="Project details">
        <ol>
          <li data-reveal><div class="si-row"><span class="si-n">Type</span><span class="si-t">Website Concept</span></div></li>
          <li data-reveal><div class="si-row"><span class="si-n">Industry</span><span class="si-t">Interior Design / Creative Services</span></div></li>
          <li data-reveal><div class="si-row"><span class="si-n">Role</span><span class="si-t">Website Design &amp; Front-End Development</span></div></li>
          <li data-reveal><div class="si-row"><span class="si-n">Platform</span><span class="si-t">Systeme.io</span></div></li>
          <li data-reveal><div class="si-row"><span class="si-n">Development</span><span class="si-t">Custom HTML, CSS &amp; JavaScript</span></div></li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ab ab-dark pj cs-open" id="overview" aria-labelledby="overview-title">
      <div class="ab-in">
        <div class="ab-split">
          <header class="ab-head">
            <p class="ab-k" data-rise>Overview</p>
            <h2 class="cs-h2" id="overview-title">Letting the work speak before the first consultation.</h2>
          </header>
          <div class="ab-body">
            <p class="ab-lead" data-rise>For an interior design studio, the website is part of the portfolio. Visitors want to see the studio’s aesthetic, understand its services, and get a sense of the work before deciding whether to make contact.</p><p data-rise>This website concept explores a more considered way to present an interior design business online, using visual storytelling, structured content, and a layout that gives the work room to stand out.</p>
            <div class="pj-actions" data-rise><a class="cta cta-menu" href="https://madinterior.systeme.io/3603c0bc" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span>View Live Concept</span><span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span><svg width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-up-right"/></svg></a></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <figure class="pj-shot cs-shot" style="--ar:16 / 9"><a class="pj-link" href="https://madinterior.systeme.io/3603c0bc" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><img src="assets/img/project-omega.webp" alt="Interior design website concept: the homepage headline reads Luxury Minimalist Interior Design For Modern Living, over a night photo of a modern house." width="1280" height="720" decoding="async"><span class="pj-hint" aria-hidden="true">View live</span></a><figcaption>Homepage screenshot of the live concept</figcaption></figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ab ab-white cs-sec" id="challenge" aria-labelledby="challenge-title">
      <div class="ab-in">
        <div class="ab-split">
          <header class="ab-head">
            <p class="ab-k" data-rise>The Design Challenge</p>
            <h2 class="cs-h2" id="challenge-title">Presenting a visual service through more than beautiful images.</h2>
          </header>
          <div class="ab-body">
            <p class="ab-lead" data-rise>Interior design is a visual discipline, but a website still needs to communicate more than aesthetics.</p><p data-rise>Visitors need to understand the studio’s approach, the services it offers, and the kind of projects it can take on. If the presentation is difficult to navigate, even strong visuals can lose their impact.</p><p data-rise>The design focused on three priorities:</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <ul class="cs-points"><li data-rise><h3>Visual storytelling</h3><p>give imagery and project presentation a meaningful role in the experience.</p></li><li data-rise><h3>Service clarity</h3><p>help visitors understand the studio’s offerings without overwhelming the page.</p></li><li data-rise><h3>Brand consistency</h3><p>create a cohesive visual direction that supports the studio’s identity.</p></li></ul>
        <div class="cs-after"><p data-rise>The objective was to create a website that feels considered while remaining practical to use.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ab ab-amber cs-sec" id="direction" aria-labelledby="direction-title">
      <span class="ab-bar ab-bar-l" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <div class="ab-in">
        <div class="ab-split">
          <header class="ab-head">
            <p class="ab-k" data-rise>The Visual Direction</p>
            <h2 class="cs-h2" id="direction-title">A layout that gives the imagery room to work.</h2>
          </header>
          <div class="ab-body">
            <p class="ab-lead" data-rise>The design direction places emphasis on composition, visual hierarchy, and the relationship between text and imagery.</p><p data-rise>Instead of treating every section as an interchangeable content block, the layout uses spacing, image placement, and typography to establish a more deliberate rhythm.</p><p data-rise>Key considerations included:</p>
            <ul class="cs-list" data-rise><li><svg width="22" height="22" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>A strong opening section that introduces the studio’s visual identity.</span></li><li><svg width="22" height="22" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Image-led sections that support the presentation of interior spaces.</span></li><li><svg width="22" height="22" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Clear typography to separate services, descriptions, and supporting information.</span></li><li><svg width="22" height="22" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Balanced spacing to avoid overcrowding the visual content.</span></li><li><svg width="22" height="22" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Consistent styling across the page to maintain a recognizable identity.</span></li></ul>
            <p data-rise>The goal was to make the website feel like an extension of the studio’s design sensibility.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ab ab-dark cs-sec" id="development" aria-labelledby="development-title">
      <div class="ab-in">
        <div class="ab-split">
          <header class="ab-head">
            <p class="ab-k" data-rise>The Development</p>
            <h2 class="cs-h2" id="development-title">Building the presentation around the design direction.</h2>
          </header>
          <div class="ab-body">
            <p class="ab-lead" data-rise>The concept was developed using Systeme.io, with custom front-end code to control the visual presentation and responsive behavior.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <ul class="dm-rows cs-tools"><li><h3 data-rise>Systeme.io</h3><div data-rise><p>Used as the website platform and publishing environment.</p></div></li><li><h3 data-rise>Custom HTML &amp; CSS</h3><div data-rise><p>Used to refine the page structure, image layouts, typography, and responsive styling.</p></div></li><li><h3 data-rise>JavaScript</h3><div data-rise><p>Used for custom interface behavior where required.</p></div></li></ul>
        <div class="cs-after"><p data-rise>The development approach allowed the design to move beyond the platform’s standard section layouts while keeping the website manageable within its publishing environment.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ab ab-white cs-sec" id="build" aria-labelledby="build-title">
      <div class="ab-in">
        <div class="ab-split">
          <header class="ab-head">
            <p class="ab-k" data-rise>What Went Into the Build</p>
            <h2 class="cs-h2" id="build-title">Design decisions translated into a working website concept.</h2>
          </header>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-table" data-rise><table><caption class="sr-only">Interior Design Website: what went into the build</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Area</th><th scope="col">Implementation</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Visual direction</th><td>Interior design-inspired art direction</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Layout</th><td>Image-led content composition</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Content structure</th><td>Studio and service information</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Typography</th><td>Clear hierarchy and editorial presentation</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Front-end</th><td>Custom HTML, CSS and JavaScript</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Platform</th><td>Systeme.io</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Responsive design</th><td>Adapted layouts for desktop and mobile</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ab ab-dark cs-sec" id="result" aria-labelledby="result-title">
      <div class="ab-in">
        <div class="ab-split">
          <header class="ab-head">
            <p class="ab-k" data-rise>The Result</p>
            <h2 class="cs-h2" id="result-title">A portfolio-led presentation for a design-focused business.</h2>
          </header>
          <div class="ab-body">
            <p class="ab-lead" data-rise>The interior design concept demonstrates how a service business can use its website to communicate both its work and its offering.</p><p data-rise>It brings together image-led presentation, organized service information, and a consistent visual direction to create an experience that supports how visitors explore and evaluate a design studio.</p>
            <p class="cs-note" data-rise><em>This is an independent website concept, not a commissioned client project. It does not represent verified business results or performance data.</em></p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <nav class="cs-next" aria-label="More case studies" data-rise>
          <a href="projects.html#interior-design-website"><span class="cs-next-k">All projects</span><span class="cs-next-t">Back to the project overview</span></a>
          <a href="case-brightwater-legal.html"><span class="cs-next-k">Next case study</span><span class="cs-next-t">Brightwater Legal</span><svg width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ab ab-amber ab-cta" id="lets-talk" aria-labelledby="talk-title">
      <span class="ab-bar ab-bar-l" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="ab-bar ab-bar-r" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <div class="ab-in">
        <h2 class="cs-cta-h" id="talk-title">Your Work Deserves a Website That Presents It Well.</h2>
        <div class="ab-cta-body">
          <p class="ab-lead" data-rise>If your business depends on the quality of your work, your website should make that quality easier to see and understand.</p>
          <p data-rise>I design and develop custom websites that bring your work, services, and business identity together in a clear online presentation.</p>
          <div class="ab-cta-actions" data-rise>
            <a class="cta cta-solid" href="https://calendly.com/-aldrichmatthew/15mins"><span>Book a Free Strategy Call</span><svg width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a>
            <a class="cta cta-ghost" href="projects.html"><span>Explore More Projects</span><svg width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

  
</Base>
